# Coverage Report

Distinguishes genuinely isolated services from those whose outbound edges could not be resolved.

| Service | Classification | Outbound edges | Detected | Resolved | Unresolved | Outside snapshot | External |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| api | isolated | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
| consumer | connected | 1 | 4 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 2 |

`isolated` means no outbound call resolved and none is left open: every detected call site, if any, goes to a third-party host (`External`) or a declared target. A leaf in this snapshot, not a gap in enola's resolution.
